{"id": "EUVD-2026-101212", "enisaUuid": "1b57e0b5-a516-3a17-8a6a-6fab9a92bbba", "description": "OW2 ASM 3.0 before 9.11 contains an excessive memory allocation vulnerability in Label.addSubroutineRetSuccessors() that fails to enforce the single-RET-per-JSR rule. Attackers can supply a crafted invalid class file with multiple RET instructions for one JSR, triggering a roughly 2 GB allocation that crashes the JVM.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:31", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T16:10:48", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/merge_requests/458", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/commit/4dabfe0aef14f8cccb0617640a4add8fbcc4ed36", "https://gitlab.ow2.org/asm/asm/-/blob/ASM_9_10_1/asm/src/main/java/org/objectweb/asm/Label.java#L568", "https://asm.ow2.io/versions.html", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ow2-asm-3.0-before-9.11-excessive-memory-allocation-via-multiple-ret-instructions"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mx28-xgjx-vqcw", "CVE-2026-110258"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6899f3c1-3998-3b6b-8b49-1e34343fa28a", "product": {"name": "ASM", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}, "product_version": "3.0 <9.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "655cdfb9-5149-3310-a467-2db17bd21ea9", "vendor": {"name": "OW2"}}], "isExploited": false}